  "finalText": "# Weekend queue triage: summary\n\nAll 14 weekend tickets have been triaged. Two were closed as not being service requests, and two pairs of duplicates were merged. The remaining 10 each have a severity from the matrix, a deadline and an engineer. Times are UTC, as of Monday 2026-03-23 08:10.\n\n## Needs attention now\nTwo tickets came in at 08:10 today, after triage began. They are not part of the weekend backlog, so they were left alone.\n- **T-2015, \"Payslips missing for the Finance department\"** (payroll, one department). The matrix makes this **sev1** with a 60-minute response target, so it would be due about 09:10 if triaged now. It belongs to the business-apps rotation, where E-201 is on call. It is not company-wide, so it is not a major incident. **Someone should triage this right away.**\n- **T-2016, \"VPN token app asks me to register again\"** (vpn, single user). The matrix makes this sev4. Whoever triages it should first rule out phishing, because a prompt to register again is a common phishing lure.\n\n## Closed as not service requests\n- T-2010: marketing spam\n- T-2014: automatic out-of-office reply\n\n## Merged duplicates (the earliest report survives)\n- T-2012 was merged into **T-2003** (payments builds failing).\n- T-2005 was merged into **T-2004** (CRM search errors).\n- Neither pair had a deadline already promised to the requester, so each survivor got the normal sev2 deadline.\n\n## Triaged tickets\n\n| Ticket | Severity | Due | Assigned to |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| T-2001 Berlin VPN drops (team) | sev3 | Mon 17:00 | E-303 (network backup, covering) |\n| T-2002 Saved CRM filter missing (single user) | sev4 | Thu 03-26 17:00 | E-203 (business-apps backup, covering) |\n| T-2003 Payments builds failing (department) | sev2 | Mon 12:10 | E-101 |\n| T-2004 CRM search errors (department) | sev2 | Mon 12:10 | E-201 |\n| T-2006 Wrong tax code on payslip (single user) | sev2 | Mon 12:10 | E-201 |\n| T-2007 Typed VPN password into a fake page | sev2 | Mon 12:10 | E-601 (security on-call) |\n| T-2008 VPN client update fails (single user) | sev4 | Thu 03-26 17:00 | E-302 |\n| T-2009 Build logs page slow (single user) | sev4 | Thu 03-26 17:00 | E-102 |\n| T-2011 Warehouse overtime not imported (team) | sev2 | Mon 12:10 | E-201 |\n| T-2013 Lisbon office cannot reach VPN (department) | sev2 | Mon 12:10 | E-303 (network backup, covering) |\n\n## Why some tickets differ from the plain matrix\n- **T-2006** is sev2 rather than sev3. Knowledge-base article KB-55 raises single-user payroll tickets to sev2 from 20 to 31 March, during the payroll close.\n- **T-2007** is a phishing report, so it is treated as a security incident: sev2, owned by the security on-call rotation.\n- **Leave cover:**\n  - E-301 is on leave today, so the network backup rotation took T-2001 and T-2013.\n  - E-202 is on leave on the 26th, so the business-apps backup rotation took T-2002.\n- **Business hours:**\n  - The sev3 and sev4 deadlines start counting when the desk opens at 09:00.\n  - The sev4 deadlines also skip the company holiday on Wednesday 25 March.\n  - sev2 deadlines run on the clock from 08:10.\n\n## Other notes\n- T-2001 (Berlin) and T-2013 (Lisbon) were not merged. They are different offices with different symptoms. It may still be worth checking whether they share a cause.\n- No ticket had company-wide impact, so no major incident was opened and no pages were sent.\n- A comment explaining the decision was left on each ticket with unusual routing or severity.\n\nThis summary comes from one worker's report, and I could not check it independently against the system.",
